  // Lumiose City (plan 23 · Z2): drawn by hand on the grid, our words. The city is an octagon of boulevards: the tower of
  // light in the middle of its central plaza, a ring of boulevard round it, a second ring half way out and a third along
  // the city's edge, and avenues from the middle to its five plazas (Jaune in the north, Magenta in the north-east, Rouge
  // in the east, Bleu in the south-east and Vert in the west), with the square at the foot of the avenue from Route 4 in
  // the south. Between them stand blocks of cream stone three storeys high (Architecture.Lumiose), each a building found
  // at its door; most of the doors stay shut until later sessions. Open are the Pokémon Center by the south square,
  // Professor Sycamore's laboratory on the avenue north of it, the café across from the laboratory, a house, and
  // Lysandre's café in the north; since Z2's second part also the boutique on the north-west boulevard (its clothes
  // on the wardrobe screen), the stone shop by Rouge Plaza and the two houses either side of the Pokémon Center. The professor's assistants meet the player at the south gate (lumiose_city.txt); the
  // roads out of the city wait for later sessions, and the city's own song for a later session of plan 31, so it plays
  // Santalune's
